   "doc": "Exactly `pq::launch_window_is_valid` (i128 arithmetic in the program,\nbigint here: no overflow) at a plausible `nowSecs`: an attestation landing\nat `nowSecs` records the window `[notBefore, notAfter]`. `nowSecs` is\nchecked like every \"now\" (TypeError for a `number`, RangeError outside i64\nor for milliseconds); `notBefore` and `notAfter` must be bigints\n(TypeError); false for window ends outside i64 (the program cannot\nreceive them).",
   "notes": "The attested window, in bigint unix seconds. `launchWindowIsValid` is exactly the program's `pq::launch_window_is_valid` for an attestation landing at `nowSecs` (60..=3,600 s long, at least 60 s of it left when it lands: `max(nowSecs, notBefore) + 60 <= notAfter`, opening at most 7 days later), and `launchWindowProblems` explains it (empty exactly when valid). `inLaunchWindow`: `launch` runs only inside it, both ends inclusive. `validateLaunchWindow` checks before signing, allowing `landingMarginSecs` (default `ATTEST_LANDING_MARGIN_SECS`, 300 s) to land with 60 s of the window left. `defaultLaunchWindow`: `[opensAt, opensAt + 3,600]`.",
