   "name": "launchWindowProblems",
   "kind": "function",
   "module": "launch/window",
   "group": "launch-flow",
   "signature": "function launchWindowProblems(nowSecs: bigint, notBefore: bigint, notAfter: bigint): string[]",
   "doc": "Why an attestation landing at `nowSecs` would NOT record this window\n(`pq::launch_window_is_valid`, exactly): it must last 60..=3,600 s, must\nhave at least 60 s left (`max(nowSecs, notBefore) + 60 <= notAfter`) and\nmust open at most 7 days after it lands. Empty exactly when `launchWindowIsValid` is true. `nowSecs` is\nchecked like every \"now\" (a `number` is a TypeError; outside i64 or\nlooking like milliseconds, a RangeError); `notBefore` and `notAfter` must\nbe bigints (TypeError), and window ends outside i64 are one problem; an\ninvalid window whose values look like milliseconds says so. A signature\nover an invalid window lands only to burn its leaf, so never sign one, and\nleave time to land (`validateLaunchWindow`).",
   "notes": "The attested window, in bigint unix seconds. `launchWindowIsValid` is exactly the program's `pq::launch_window_is_valid` for an attestation landing at `nowSecs` (60..=3,600 s long, at least 60 s of it left when it lands: `max(nowSecs, notBefore) + 60 <= notAfter`, opening at most 7 days later), and `launchWindowProblems` explains it (empty exactly when valid). `inLaunchWindow`: `launch` runs only inside it, both ends inclusive. `validateLaunchWindow` checks before signing, allowing `landingMarginSecs` (default `ATTEST_LANDING_MARGIN_SECS`, 300 s) to land with 60 s of the window left. `defaultLaunchWindow`: `[opensAt, opensAt + 3,600]`.",
