   "kind": "function",
   "module": "metadata/png",
   "group": "metadata",
   "signature": "function pngInfo(bytes: Uint8Array): PngInfo",
   "doc": "The header of the PNG `bytes`, after checking its structure: the\nsignature, chunks whose lengths stay inside the file and whose CRC-32s\nmatch, IHDR first (13 bytes; width and height 1..2^31-1, a valid colour\ntype and bit depth), IDAT present, IEND last with nothing after it.\nThrows `PngError` otherwise. It does not inflate the image data.",
   "notes": "A small palette PNG for the icon (32x32 with 16 colours is about 130 to 700 bytes): RGBA quantized deterministically (or `{ indices, palette }` as given), the smallest bit depth, tRNS only when needed, IDAT through `CompressionStream(\"deflate\")` when available and smaller, else stored. The same input gives the same bytes on one platform (`\"store\"`: on every platform); keep the bytes that were signed. `pngInfo` checks a PNG's structure (signature, CRCs, IHDR first, IEND last).",
