   "doc": "After the user confirmed it (audit 4, ID-F1c: \"this key was used\nelsewhere\"), record every leaf `used` shows that this ledger never signed\nat as taken, so new signatures can be made again: a leaf without a record\ngets a `burned` record with no message, a `reserved` record that never\nsigned is marked burned. `expectedCount` must equal the number of such\nleaves now (`UnknownLeavesError.unknownCount`, as shown to the user), so a\nconfirmation never covers leaves the user did not see. Only confirm when\nno other device holds signatures of this identity that have not landed\n(better: import its records, `importLeafRecords`).",
   "notes": "Audit round 4, ID-F1c (both also at the package root). The signers refuse, before anything is reserved, while the identity's bitmap shows leaves this ledger never signed at. Import the other device's records first. Only when the user confirms that every signature made elsewhere has landed, record those leaves as taken with `acknowledgeUnknownLeaves`, passing the count the user saw (`unknownCount`): a different count is refused. A very large count is a sign of a lying RPC: do not confirm it.",
