   "group": "pq-identity",
   "signature": "function confirmAttestation(\n  conn: Connection,\n  launch: PublicKey,\n  expectedMessageHash: Uint8Array,\n  opts: ConfirmAttestationOptions = {},\n): Promise<AttestationOutcome>",
   "doc": "Whether `launch` is attested by the message with SHA-256\n`expectedMessageHash`: its attestation must have version 3 and hold that\nhash. Otherwise, given `leaf` and `lmsPublicKey`, a set leaf bit means the\nlanding only burned the leaf (`burned`, with `burnReasons`: the empty\nversion-0 attestation of `PqLeafConsumed`, or another message's); a clear\none means it has not landed (`pending`). With `ledger`, the leaf's record\nis updated: `markLanded` (attested or not) when it holds a signature,\n`markBurned` when it was only reserved (something else set the bit).",
   "notes": "`attested` only when the attestation holds this message's hash; `burned` (with `reasons`: `record-missing`, `rules-missing`, `invalid-window`, `wrong-identity`, `already-attested`) when the leaf was used without attesting; `pending` when nothing landed. Never assume a landing attested.",
