   "signature": "function fundingLamportsForPending(\n  conn: Connection,\n  args: Omit<LandOrBurnPendingArgs, \"payer\" | \"burnOnly\" | \"allowLocalnet\"> & { readonly count?: number | undefined },\n): Promise<bigint>",
   "doc": "Lamports a throwaway payer needs to land `count` pending signatures (default:\nall of them): the fees, the rent of the accounts a landing creates if they\ndo not exist yet, and, for more than one landing, the rent-exempt minimum\nthe payer must keep between them (return it with `buildSweepPayerTx`).",
   "notes": "Re-sends the pending signatures with their recorded bytes (never a new signature), from a funded throwaway `payer`: each attests or only burns its leaf, and the ledger records it. Burns are marked `retired` and do not count against `maxBurnOnlyLandings`. With `burnOnly: true` only those that would just burn their leaf are landed: run it while the launch's attestation holds the slot. After the window passed, without `burnOnly`, those that only burn land first, then the newest that can attest.",
